  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment should establish a strong multimodal baseline using the most sophisticated components across all design axes: multiprofile (richer than singleprofile), scvi_n200 (well-validated RNA encoder), imagenet_vit_l (stronger image encoder than resnet50), transformer aggregation (more expressive than avgpool), and weighted fusion (principled combination). This 'full-stack' configuration tests the core hypothesis that multimodal fusion with advanced components outperforms simpler alternatives. If it performs well, it sets a high ceiling and subsequent experiments can ablate or swap individual components (e.g., scgpt vs scvi, concat vs weighted, resnet50 vs ViT-L) to identify what drives performance. If it underperforms, it signals that the complexity is harmful and we should pivot toward simpler configurations. This maximizes information gain per experiment under a tight budget of 10."
}

